Package: fastIWTlm
Type: Package
Title: Fast Interval-Wise Testing for Functional Regression with ggplot2 Visualisation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Matteo", "Fontana", email = "mtt.fnt@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("fastIWTlm", "contributors", role = "ctb"))
Description: Interval-Wise Testing (IWT) for functional data. Provides
    functional-on-scalar and functional-on-functional regression via
    'fastIWTlm()', a high-performance C++/Rcpp permutation engine for the
    two-sample problem via 'fastIWT2()' (RcppEigen, OpenMP-parallelised), a
    pure-R two-sample implementation 'IWT2()', base-graphics heatmaps via
    'IWTimage()', and a 'ggplot2'-based visualisation layer for 'IWTlm'
    objects ('autoplot.IWTlm()' and 'arrange_IWTlm()'). The permutation loop
    of 'fastIWTlm()' can optionally be dispatched to a parallel RcppEigen
    kernel via 'engine = "rcpp"'. This package merges the former 'fastIWTlm'
    (computation) and 'IWTgg' (plotting) repositories.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppEigen
Imports:
